  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "unspecified",
    "description": "sfxnz's two-DGX-Spark vLLM TP2 recipe (upstream commit 072c3f68, 2026-09-28) for the official nvidia/GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4 ModelOpt checkpoint (snapshot 09b04e5e, MIT) with the incoai GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2 block-diffusion drafter (snapshot 7d74cdd8, CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0: non-commercial, no derivatives) drafting 7 tokens per step. The image bakes upstream's whole glm53-sm121-v8 to v13 patch chain byte-identically on the digest-pinned vllm/vllm-openai glm53-flash-arm64-cu130 base: sm_121 sparse-MLA and FP8 KV, DFlash2 backport (vLLM PR 52816), GLM5-Next aux-hidden capture and draft KV groups, and the opt-in v13 switches. Upstream's defaults are kept: drafter linears NVFP4 W4A16, target shared/MLA/KDA/lm_head linears INT8 W8A16 (g128), indexer tail-ring fix and adaptive verify at tau 0.3, FP8 KV pinned at 4.14 GiB, 327,680-token window, two sequences, CUDA graphs 1/2/4/8/16, image and video input (4 images, 1 video per prompt), thinking off by default with upstream's chat template, output capped at 65,536 tokens. Each upstream switch that needs no different weights is a recipe option with upstream's default. Not offered: upstream's SPEC=mtp lane needs the different LibertAI checkpoint (upstream refuses MTP on the nvidia pack), the DRAFT_REV drafter snapshots are different weights, and upstream's refuse-guards (more than 327,680 tokens on fp8 KV, a non-marlin MoE or linear backend, hiding the vision tower, an unpinned KV budget) stay closed. Upstream's JIT compile cache is left to the platform's cache handling. Upstream measured prose decode of 30.04 tok/s at concurrency 1 and 20.69 tok/s per stream (39.43 aggregate) at concurrency 2 on its own two-Spark lab (claims, not measured here). Licences are information only: upstream scripts MIT (sfxnz), vLLM Apache-2.0, checkpoint MIT, drafter CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0 (commercial use via inco.ai). Vonk physical two-Spark acceptance is pending.",
